  "ai": {
    "chunks": [
      "3 - He said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Umar al-Ji'abi reported to us... from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah al-Abdi, who said:",
      "When Ibn Muljam struck Amir al-Mu'minin Ali ibn Abi Talib, peace be upon him, a group of our companions went to him in the morning. We sat at the door, heard weeping, and wept too. Al-Hasan ibn Ali came out and said: 'Return to your homes.' All departed except me. I said: 'By Allah, I will not leave until I see Amir al-Mu'minin.'",
      "He paused, entered, and soon came out saying: 'Enter.' I found Amir al-Mu'minin reclining with a yellow turban, bled out and pale. I fell upon him, kissed him and wept. He said: 'Do not weep, O Asbagh, by Allah it is Paradise.' I said: 'I know you are going to Paradise. I weep because I will lose you. Narrate to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, for I may never hear from you again.'",
      "He said: 'Yes, O Asbagh. The Messenger of Allah called me one day and said: O Ali, go to my mosque, ascend my pulpit, praise Allah, invoke blessings upon me, then say: O people! I am a messenger of Allah to you. He says: The curse of Allah, His angels, His prophets, and my curse upon whoever attributes himself to other than his father, claims other than his masters, or wrongs a worker of his wages.'",
      "So I went to his mosque, ascended his pulpit, and when the Quraysh saw me, they came toward me. I praised Allah, glorified Him, blessed the Messenger, and repeated the same proclamation of curse upon the three categories of wrongdoers.",
      "No one spoke except Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: 'You have conveyed, O Abu al-Hasan, but you have come with an unexplained statement.' I said: 'I will convey that to the Messenger of Allah.' So I returned to the Prophet and informed him.",
      "He said: 'Go back to my mosque, ascend my pulpit, praise Allah, glorify Him, bless me, and say: O people! We would not bring you anything unless we have its interpretation and explanation. Verily, I am your father. Verily, I am your master. Verily, I am the one employed for you.'"
    ],
